Proxy matlab ek aise cheez jo kisi ko intercept kar pa rahi hai.

Let say we have an user service that use one order service method and we want to log each and every activity of user
like when he placed an order, what order he placed , so what we can do is we can create a proxy which can intercept each
 of the activity performed by the user, so whenever user is ordering or doing something the proxy will intercept it
 (think like middleware in nodejs) and after that only call is forwarded to other required service.


 Proxy can be used to add log, cache result , etc.

 In technical terms proxy is a object that stands in front of another object and control access to it.

 Means instead of service.doWork() we call proxy.doWork();

Types of proxy

1.Static Proxy-: A static proxy is a proxy class that is written manually by the developer.

2. Dynamic Proxy -: These proxy are created at runtime by Java and it's framework . We do not write proxy class manually
 here.
These are of 2 types.

A. JDK Dynamic Proxy -:It only works when a class implements a interface.

B. CGLIB Proxy -: Used when class does not implement interface.